SCHEMA_VERSION='product-identity/v3'
PROMPT = ('Check the first image independently against the declared product and supplied visual evidence. '
          'Return schema_version=product-identity/v3, task_type, item_id, decision MATCH/MISMATCH/UNCERTAIN, '
          'confidence, abstain, evidence_ids, and observations. observations MUST contain product_subject, image_type, '
          'model_identity, color, packaging. Each contains value, decision, confidence, abstain, evidence_ids. '
          'image_type.value is BOX/FIGURE/MIXED/UNCERTAIN. BOX includes windowed retail packaging even if the enclosed toy is visible; '
          'MIXED means an unpackaged product outside its box alongside packaging. packaging.value is BOXED/UNBOXED/MIXED/UNCERTAIN. '
          'model_identity additionally requires visibility VISIBLE/NOT_VISIBLE/NOT_VERIFIABLE. '
          'When a model is not visible or cannot be proved, set value=null, decision=UNCERTAIN and preserve that reason; '
          'do not guess a catalog code, and do not turn absence into a mismatch. '
          'Each observation needs its own actual confidence and bound evidence_ids. '
          'Keep image type, subject and packaging observations even if color/model is uncertain. '
          'A model code requires model_evidence_ids referencing supplied evidence (or the model_identity evidence_ids). Never infer an unsupported model.')
